(Diabetes management requires continuous monitoring of blood glucose levels to prevent dangerous) Tj
T* (events such as hypoglycemia and hyperglycemia. Existing prediction systems are often designed for) Tj
T* (individual patients, have limited generalization across populations, and rely heavily on cloud) Tj
T* (computing, leading to latency and privacy concerns. This project aims to develop a Transformer-based) Tj
T* (population-specific blood glucose prediction system that leverages Continuous Glucose Monitoring) Tj
T* (\(CGM\) data and patient demographic information for accurate multi-horizon glucose forecasting. The) Tj
T* (proposed model utilizes a Temporal Fusion Transformer \(TFT\) to capture temporal dependencies and) Tj
T* (personalize predictions based on static patient characteristics. The trained model is deployed on a) Tj
T* (low-power wearable edge device to provide real-time glucose predictions without requiring continuous) Tj
T* (internet connectivity. This enables timely medical interventions, reduces the risk of adverse glycemic) Tj
T* (events, and improves diabetes management for both Type 1 and Type 2 diabetes patients.) Tj
ET
